The Thirteenth Realm is a hidden realm that orbits [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]] and its twin [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|Ilkyne]], separate from the twelve [[Geography/Althane/Realms/index|realms]] Lacuna made. [[Org/Althane/Church of the Thirteenth Realm|The Church of the Thirteenth Realm]] preaches it as a paradise.

The realm holds the machinery of the [[Phenomena/Althane/Cycle|cycle]] and a warden who keeps its records. It steers seekers away from ways of ascending that earlier cycles already tried, so no cycle is spent repeating a failure, and keeps a full list of every attempt. Breaking the realm and walking out of [[Divinity/Immix|the Lighthouse]] alive is the test of whether a mortal has grown strong enough to kill a [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]], and the [[Org/The Fifth Prosperous Empire of the Sundom|Sundom]] built its experiment on that mark. The Leviathan can be steered remotely from the Thirteenth Realm, which is why the Brejvasens grow a living brain into its works to move it instead.
